    "field": "Climate dynamics",
    "problem": "The complexity of the coupled ocean-atmosphere system, along with natural variability and land-sea distribution, makes it challenging to determine the specific causal mechanisms driving the observed poleward shift of climate zones under global warming.",
    "method": "The paper uses an idealized coupled aqua-planet model with a series of partially coupled experiments to isolate and quantify the distinct contributions of direct CO\u2082 forcing, indirect ocean surface warming, and wind-stress feedback to the poleward shift of atmospheric and oceanic circulation.",
    "task": "The task is to decode the dynamics of the poleward shift in climate zones using idealized aqua-planet model simulations to isolate the contributing roles of direct CO2 forcing and indirect ocean surface warming.",
